<http://data.silknow.org/event/1a1f7ade-cb20-390e-8a4c-21f1b825b603>
        a                              ecrm:E8_Acquisition ;
        rdfs:comment                   "The playbill was printed for the opening of a season at the Tae-Ming Theatre, Shanghai, on 8th March 1854, under the management of Horatio Buskin, and would have been commissioned by him. The two plays performed that evening by the British company were <i>A Fast Train-High Pressure-Express</i> performed by Horatio Buskin, John Pritt Harley and Mr. Tupman, and <i>The Practical Man</i> by Mr. Tupman, Frank Matthews, Horatio Buskin, Mr. Poster, Paul Bedford, Julia Bennett, and Priscilla Horton. The orchestra was conducted by Messrs Thalberg and Konig; the scenery was by Clarkson Stanfield, and dresses and properties by Mlle Rigolette Bellefille. The programme announced ths forthcoming productions <i>Diamond Cut Diamond</i> and <i>I've Eaten My Friend.</i> The programme was given to the museum in December 1961 by Mrs. M.R.T. Momber"@en ;
        ecrm:P14_carried_out_by        <http://data.silknow.org/actor/2523033f-49c9-33cd-999d-496417263ddd> ;
        ecrm:P22_transferred_title_to  <http://data.silknow.org/actor/f0577f91-f887-3019-bf88-f9e5ba019390> ;
        ecrm:P23_transferred_title_from
                "Given by Mrs. M.R.T. Momber" ;
        ecrm:P24_transferred_title_of  <http://data.silknow.org/object/e94335ef-e07f-3d9d-86ab-6a927dbba3a2> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "The playbill was printed for the opening of a season at the Tae-Ming Theatre, Shanghai, on 8th March 1854, under the management of Horatio Buskin, and would have been commissioned by him. The two plays performed that evening by the British company were <i>A Fast Train-High Pressure-Express</i> performed by Horatio Buskin, John Pritt Harley and Mr. Tupman, and <i>The Practical Man</i> by Mr. Tupman, Frank Matthews, Horatio Buskin, Mr. Poster, Paul Bedford, Julia Bennett, and Priscilla Horton. The orchestra was conducted by Messrs Thalberg and Konig; the scenery was by Clarkson Stanfield, and dresses and properties by Mlle Rigolette Bellefille. The programme announced ths forthcoming productions <i>Diamond Cut Diamond</i> and <i>I've Eaten My Friend.</i> The programme was given to the museum in December 1961 by Mrs. M.R.T. Momber"@en .
